(2013) concluded that the novel Of Mice and Men helps capture this exploitation and
alienation. The workers labour themselves 11 hours a day for 6 days a week, to be paid
insufficiently. The capitalist mode of production allows the capitalist to reduce the worker to
a mere commodity.

In conclusion, we come to see that the commodity form breathes exploitation through the
abstraction of value, the stealing of surplus value, the tendency of the rate of profit to fall
creating even more exploitation and the alienation of the worker from both their labour and
the world at large.

